notes               = "Untitled in source. IMPORTANT — the ===lantern=== on this poem is BEN'S OWN pencil rendering from the margin of the printed page, dated '3/22/26', not an agent's; his parenthetical '(is)' is reproduced as written. This follows the page-70 / stay-go precedent that lantern can hold a human draft. Note he turns من درختم ('I am a tree') into 'the tree in me' and moves the restless green to the head of the colour list, where the printed order is yellow, blue, green; the literal machine pass keeps the Persian order. The date gives a month but no day (۱۳۷۵/۸, Aban), month 8 → +621 = 1996. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

من درختم
زرد خورشید
آبی آب
سبز بی‌تاب
و
برگ برگ چشم‌هایم
پُر از شوقی ناب...
۱۳۷۵/۸

===machine===

I am a tree —
the yellow of the sun,
the blue of water,
restless green,
and
leaf by leaf my eyes
full of a pure longing...
1375/8

===lantern===

The tree
in me
(is) restless green
sun-glow yellow
& watery blue

Leaf by leaf
my eyes
swollen with
raw ardor

